From 9afaa6bf054ffcdb882e33a1ce2ed32c86866977 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LCCC Contributor <lccc@ms178.github.io>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] passes, loop_idiom: fold Brian Kernighan bit-clear loops
 into popcount

Recognize `while (x) { x &= x - 1; ++n; }` and guarded `do { x &= x - 1; ++n; } while (x)`
loops in `loop_idiom` (`try_match_popcount_loop` / `rewrite_popcount_loop`) and
replace the loop with `IrUnaryOp::Popcount(x)` plus any non-zero initial
accumulator value when `Driver::resolved_fast_popcount()` confirms the active
target emits native hardware popcount instructions without a libcall and
`-ftrapv` / `-fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns` are not active.

Refs: docs/PERFORMANCE-BACKLOG.md, OP-16
