From: LCCC Contributor <lccc@ms178.github.io>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] passes, backend: narrow CRC32 table indices, bitop
 bounds, and i686 cast loads

1. Canonicalize narrow unsigned casts (`Cast(U8|U16 -> I32|U32|I64|U64)` and
   `Cast(U8|U16 -> I32) -> Cast(I32 -> I64)`) feeding scaled CRC table GEP
   offsets in `bit_idioms::canonicalize_narrow_crc_casts` into explicit `And`
   masks in the widened integer type, and extend `fits_low_bits` across
   narrow unsigned casts and two-operand `Xor`/`Or`.
2. Extend `integer_bounds` across unsigned casts and two-operand `And`/`Xor`/`Or`,
   fold redundant low-bit masks (`And(x, mask) -> Copy(x)` when `max(x) <= mask`),
   forward same-width sign-changing casts on `<= i32::MAX` bounded sources,
   collapse `64 -> 32 -> 64` round-trip casts on `[0, i32::MAX]` bounded
   64-bit sources (eliminating `movl %eax, %esi` in `k17_popcnt64.c`), retype
   single-use `I32` bitwise defs to `U32` when feeding widened casts, and run
   `copy_prop` + `dce` when `integer_bounds` mutates the IR.
3. Compute a forward closure `collect_bitop_nonneg_values` over `And`/`Or`/`Xor`/`LShr`
   of known non-negative 32-bit values and thread `bitop_nonneg_values` into
   `ensure_sib_index_form` and `emit_sext32_for_value` so x86-64 SIB addressing
   uses the zero-extended 32-bit sub-register directly without `movslq`.
4. Stage commutative `%rax` RHS operands directly into `dest_phys` in
   `emit_alu_reg_direct` when `lhs != dest`, reducing `crc32_nibble_hot.c` inner
   loops from 10 to 8 instructions (matching GCC 16.2).
5. Consult `narrow_images` in i686 `emit_cast_impl` so widening casts of
   already sign-/zero-extended sub-word loads elide redundant `movsbl`/`movzbl`
   re-extensions and register relays (`check_load_widen_cast_no_relay.sh`).

