From d7e7fd1460c728d637fbd8da67bf2aa80c81740a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LCCC Contributor <lccc@ms178.github.io>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] driver, x86/peephole: cut -O1/-O2 compile-time Ir on
 register-heavy functions

1. Pre-parse up to two register family tags (`reg_refs: [u8; 2]`) and store the
   trimmed line start offset (`trim_start: u16`) once in `LineInfo::from_line`
   and `update_line`, avoiding repeated full-line byte scans in
   `scan_forward_reg_ref`, `line_references_reg_fast`, `has_implicit_reg_usage`,
   `find_And_eliminate_unused_callee_saves`, and `eliminate_dead_reg_moves`.
2. Add a bitmask fast-reject in `eliminate_dead_stores` before calling
   `classify_rbp_Zero_disp` on instructions that never reference `%rbp`, and
   skip `fold_memory_operands` / `propagate_register_copies` iterations on
   functions with no frame accesses or register-to-register moves.
3. Use `DualLayout::ChainOnly` at `opt_level <= 1` in `Driver::compile_module_ir`
   instead of running codegen twice per function during `-O1` compiles, and wire
   `Driver::resolved_fast_popcount()` into `loop_idiom`.
4. Reduces Callgrind Ir on `expat_siphash24.c` by -55.8% at `-O1`
   (3.384G -> 1.495G Ir) and -15.5% at `-O2` (1.408G -> 1.190G Ir).

Refs: MS-20, OP-16
